# Moon-Circuit Hacker: "you may draw a card. If you do, discard a card unless this creature entered this turn." Bot1 attacks
# on turn 3 with Ornithopter (power 0), unblocked; in the declare blockers step Mox Sapphire pays Ninjutsu {U} and the Hacker
# comes in tapped and attacking in its place (CR 702.49a). It deals 2 to Bot2 the turn it entered: Bot1 draws and discards
# nothing (hand 6 -> 7, graveyard empty). The control, a Hacker that entered on an earlier turn, is
# moon-circuit-hacker-on-a-later-turn-loots.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Sapphire
Ornithopter
Moon-Circuit Hacker
Island x4
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Ornithopter)
[T3 Bot1.Blockers]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Moon-Circuit Hacker.Activate(Ability: Ninjutsu)
Bot1.Choose(Pay mana)
Bot1.Choose(Ornithopter)
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Pass
? Bot1.Hand.Count = 6
Bot1.Accept
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 18
Bot1.Hand.Count = 7
Bot1.Graveyard.Count = 0
Bot1.Battlefield.Moon-Circuit Hacker.Tapped = true
